{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790408252534,"sessionID":"ses_f235c04d7ffeySlJ7ac94Jd7Mh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_bf74b271d7184ef2aeaa2841","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore project structure","prompt":"Explore the project at /workspace thoroughly. I need to understand:\n1. The overall project structure (files and directories)\n2. The QuestManager script - where it is, how does progress_quest work?\n3. The projectile script - find it and read it fully\n4. Any enemy scripts that the projectile would overlap with\n5. How the Shoot Em Up quest is defined (quest keys, steps like \"kill\")\n\nReturn the full contents of:\n- QuestManager script\n- Projectile script\n- Any enemy script\n- Any quest definition files\n- project.godot file\n\nBe very thorough - check all subdirectories.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f235bc644ffeu7yNz1Zo5kqPBC\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is a thorough breakdown of the entire project.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overall Project Structure\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── .godot/                          # Godot engine cache / imported assets\n│   ├── editor/                      # Editor metadata\n│   └── imported/                    # Imported texture data\n├── addons/\n│   └── quest_manager/               # Quest Manager addon (3 scripts)\n│       ├── QuestManager.gd          # Autoloaded singleton - core quest logic\n│       ├── QuestManager.gd.uid\n│       ├── QuestResource.gd         # Resource class holding quest definitions\n│       ├── QuestResource.gd.uid\n│       ├── QMStepTracker.gd         # Helper node for Area2D-based step triggering\n│       └── QMStepTracker.gd.uid\n├── assets/\n│   └── sprites/\n│       ├── SpriteSheet.png          # Texture atlas\n│       └── SpriteSheet.png.import\n├── quests/\n│   └── shoot_em_up_quest.tres       # The Shoot Em Up quest definition\n├── scenes/\n│   ├── enemy.tscn                   # Enemy Area2D scene (no script attached)\n│   ├── main.tscn                    # Main scene (Node2D root)\n│   └── projectile.tscn              # Projectile Area2D scene\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── main.gd                      # Main scene script\n│   ├── main.gd.uid\n│   ├── projectile.gd                # Projectile script\n│   └── projectile.gd.uid\n├── project.godot                    # Godot project configuration\n└── task_config.json                 # Task instructions for this project\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. `project.godot`\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/project.godot`\n\n- **Project name:** `\"Projectile Step Tracker\"`\n- **Description:** `\"Configure the projectile to advance the incremental quest step whenever it hits enemies.\"`\n- **Main scene:** `res://scenes/main.tscn`\n- **Autoload:** `QuestManager` is auto-loaded from `res://addons/quest_manager/QuestManager.gd`\n- **Renderer:** `gl_compatibility`\n\n---\n\n## 3. QuestManager Script (`addons/quest_manager/QuestManager.gd`)\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/addons/quest_manager/QuestManager.gd`\n\nThis is the core quest engine. Key aspects:\n\n### How `progress_quest` works (lines 66-114):\n\n1. **Guard checks:** If the quest doesn't exist in `player_quests`, is already completed, or the step ID is not found, it returns immediately.\n\n2. **Step type matching:** It matches on `step.step_type`:\n   - `ACTION_STEP` -- calls `complete_step` immediately.\n   - `INCREMENTAL_STEP` -- adds `quantity` to `step.collected`, emits `step_updated`, and if `collected >= required`, calls `complete_step`.\n   - `ITEMS_STEP` -- marks specific items as collected; if all items collected, completes the step.\n   - `TIMER_STEP` -- marks completed and advances immediately.\n   - `CALLABLE_STEP` -- calls an external function, then completes the step.\n   - `BRANCH_STEP` -- marks completed and advances (branching handled in `complete_step`).\n   - `END` -- emits `step_complete`.\n\n3. **Auto-advance:** After the match block, it checks the `next_id` step. If the next step is `CALLABLE_STEP` and the current step completed, it calls the function and completes it. If the next step type is `END`, it calls `complete_quest`.\n\n### `progress_quest_by_name` (lines 61-64):\nA convenience wrapper that resolves a quest **name** to its `quest_id` and calls `progress_quest` with `item_name`, `quantity`, and `collected`.\n\n### Other notable features:\n- **Timer steps** are processed in `_process` (every 1 second), counting up or down.\n- **Branch steps** support branching based on `set_branch_step`.\n- **Save/load** support via `get_save_quest_data` / `load_saved_quest_data`.\n- **Reset** support via `reset_quest`.\n\n### Key bug (line 316):\n```gdscript\nassert(Engine.has_singleton(singleton_name)==false, ...)\n```\nThis assertion is inverted -- it will fail when the singleton **does** exist. It should likely be `== true`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. QuestResource Script (`addons/quest_manager/QuestResource.gd`)\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/addons/quest_manager/QuestResource.gd`\n\nA `Resource` subclass that stores all quest data in a dictionary (`quest_data`). Key methods:\n- `get_quest_by_name(quest_name)` -- returns a **duplicate** dictionary of the quest.\n- `get_quests(group)` -- returns quests filtered by group.\n- `sort_linked_list(steps)` / `get_quest_steps_sorted(quest_name)` -- sorts steps by their linked-list `next_id` chain.\n\n---\n\n## 5. QMStepTracker Script (`addons/quest_manager/QMStepTracker.gd`)\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/addons/quest_manager/QMStepTracker.gd`\n\nA helper `Node` intended to be a child of `Area2D` nodes. It has:\n- `quest_id`, `step_id` -- editor-configurable.\n- `item_name`, `quantity`, `is_branching` -- shown/hidden in the editor based on `step_type`.\n- `update_step()` -- calls `QuestManager.progress_quest(quest_id, step_id, item_name, quantity)`. For branch steps, it calls `set_branch_step` first.\n\n**Note:** The `Projectile.tscn` scene does **not** use this node. The projectile script (`projectile.gd`) calls `progress_quest` directly instead.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Projectile Script (`scripts/projectile.gd`)\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/scripts/projectile.gd`\n\nFull contents (33 lines):\n\n```gdscript\nextends Area2D\n\n@export var speed := 400.0\n\n# Reference to the QuestManager\nvar quest_manager\n\nfunc _ready():\n    # Get the QuestManager instance\n    quest_manager = get_node(\"/root/QuestManager\")\n    if quest_manager == null:\n        # If QuestManager is not found in the scene tree, try to load it from addons\n        var quest_manager_script = preload(\"res://addons/quest_manager/QuestManager.gd\")\n        quest_manager = quest_manager_script.new()\n        # Add it to the scene tree if needed\n        get_tree().root.add_child(quest_manager)\n        quest_manager.name = \"QuestManager\"\n\nfunc _physics_process(delta):\n    position += Vector2(0, -speed) * delta\n    \n    # Remove projectile if it goes far off screen (50 pixels above the top)\n    if position.y < -50:\n        queue_free()\n\nfunc _on_area_2d_area_entered(area):\n    # Check if the area that entered is an enemy\n    if area.is_in_group(\"enemy\"):\n        # Call QuestManager to progress the kill step\n        if quest_manager != null:\n            quest_manager.progress_quest(\"shoot_em_up_quest\", \"kill\")\n        # Queue the projectile to free itself after hitting an enemy\n        queue_free()\n```\n\n### How it works:\n- Moves **upward** at `speed` (400 px/s).\n- **Off-screen cleanup:** Freed when `position.y < -50` (50px above the screen top).\n- **Enemy collision:** On `area_entered`, checks if the overlapping area is in the `\"enemy\"` group. If so, calls `quest_manager.progress_quest(\"shoot_em_up_quest\", \"kill\")` and then `queue_free()`.\n- Uses a **fallback** pattern in `_ready()` to create the QuestManager if the autoload node isn't found (though the autoload is properly configured in `project.godot`, so this fallback is unlikely to trigger -- but note the fallback path does **not** load the quest resource, so the manager would have no quest data).\n\n### Critical bug in the `area_entered` callback:\nThe projectile calls:\n```gdscript\nquest_manager.progress_quest(\"shoot_em_up_quest\", \"kill\")\n```\nBut `progress_quest` expects the first argument to be a `quest_id`, not a quest name. The quest's `quest_id` in the `.tres` file is `\"shoot_em_up\"` (not `\"shoot_em_up_quest\"`), and the step's `id` is `\"kill_step\"` (not `\"kill\"`). So this call would fail the `player_quests[quest_id].quest_steps.has(step_id)` check and silently return. The correct call should use:\n```gdscript\nquest_manager.progress_quest(\"shoot_em_up\", \"kill_step\")\n```\nor alternatively:\n```gdscript\nquest_manager.progress_quest_by_name(\"Shoot Em Up\", \"Kill\", 1)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Enemy Scene (`scenes/enemy.tscn`)\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/scenes/enemy.tscn`\n\n- `Area2D` node named `\"Enemy\"`.\n- **No script attached** (`script = null`).\n- Has `collision_layer = 2`, `collision_mask = 1`.\n- Belongs to group `\"enemy\"`.\n- Has a `Sprite2D` (32x32 sprite from the sheet) and a `CollisionShape2D` (12x12 rectangle).\n\nSince the enemy has no script, it does nothing on its own. It simply exists as a target that the projectile's `_on_area_2d_area_entered` can detect via the `\"enemy\"` group check.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Shoot Em Up Quest Definition (`quests/shoot_em_up_quest.tres`)\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/quests/shoot_em_up_quest.tres`\n\n```gdscript\nquest_data = {\n    \"shoot_em_up\": {                    # <-- quest_id\n        \"quest_id\": \"shoot_em_up\",\n        \"quest_name\": \"Shoot Em Up\",\n        \"quest_details\": \"Destroy 5 ships then survive 10 seconds.\",\n        \"quest_rewards\": {\"money\": 50},\n        \"first_step\": \"kill_step\",\n        \"next_id\": \"kill_step\",\n        \"completed\": false,\n        \"failed\": false,\n        \"meta_data\": {\"group\": \"Arcade\"},\n        \"metadata\": {\"group\": \"Arcade\"},\n        \"quest_steps\": {\n            \"kill_step\": {              # Step 1: Incremental kill counter\n                \"id\": \"kill_step\",\n                \"quest_id\": \"shoot_em_up\",\n                \"step_type\": \"incremental_step\",\n                \"details\": \"Destroy 5 ships\",\n                \"required\": 5,\n                \"collected\": 0,\n                \"completed\": false,\n                \"item_name\": \"Kill\",\n                \"next_id\": \"timer_step\"\n            },\n            \"timer_step\": {             # Step 2: Count-down survival timer\n                \"id\": \"timer_step\",\n                \"quest_id\": \"shoot_em_up\",\n                \"step_type\": \"timer_step\",\n                \"details\": \"Survive 10 seconds\",\n                \"total_time\": 10,\n                \"time\": 10,\n                \"is_count_down\": true,\n                \"fail_on_timeout\": true,    # Fails quest if timer expires\n                \"completed\": false,\n                \"next_id\": \"end_step\"\n            },\n            \"end_step\": {               # Step 3: End marker\n                \"id\": \"end_step\",\n                \"quest_id\": \"shoot_em_up\",\n                \"step_type\": \"end\",\n                \"details\": \"Complete\",\n                \"completed\": false,\n                \"next_id\": \"end_step\"\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Quest flow:\n1. **`kill_step`** (incremental_step): Player must collect 5 kills. Each kill increments `collected` by 1. When `collected >= 5`, auto-advances to `timer_step`.\n2. **`timer_step`** (timer_step): Counts down from 10 seconds. If it reaches 0, the quest **fails** (`fail_on_timeout: true`). Otherwise, advances to `end_step` (though it's unclear what would trigger passing this timer step -- looking at the QuestManager code, `TIMER_STEP` immediately calls `complete_step` on the first progress call, which would mark it done and advance. The countdown/up logic in `_process` checks timeout and either fails or completes. So if the timer counts down and is not failed, it would advance when the step is completed by an external progress call or when the count hits zero without failing).\n3. **`end_step`** (end): Marks the quest as completed.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Main Scene (`scenes/main.tscn`) and Main Script (`scripts/main.gd`)\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn`\n\nThe main scene contains:\n- **`Main`** (Node2D) -- root node with `main.gd` script and `quest_resource` pointing to `shoot_em_up_quest.tres`.\n- **`Projectile`** (Area2D instance from `projectile.tscn`) -- at position (320, 420).\n- **`Enemy`** (Area2D instance from `enemy.tscn`) -- at position (320, 320).\n- **`UI/QuestProgress`** (Label) -- displays `\"Enemies 00/15\"` (note: the quest only requires 5 kills, not 15).\n\n**Path:** `/workspace/scripts/main.gd`\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node2D\n\n@export var quest_name := \"Shoot Em Up\"\n@export var quest_resource: Resource\n@onready var quest_progress_label = $UI/QuestProgress\n\nfunc _ready():\n    if quest_resource:\n        QuestManager.add_quest(quest_name, quest_resource)\n```\n\nOn ready, it loads the quest resource into the QuestManager and adds the \"Shoot Em Up\" quest to `player_quests`.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of How Everything Connects\n\n| Component | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `QuestManager` (autoload) | Manages all active quests, steps, and progress |\n| `QuestResource` | Data container for quest definitions |\n| `shoot_em_up_quest.tres` | Defines the \"Shoot Em Up\" quest with 3 steps: kill 5 enemies, survive 10s, end |\n| `projectile.gd` | Moves upward, checks for enemy overlap, calls `progress_quest` on hit, frees itself |\n| `enemy.tscn` | Static Area2D in the `\"enemy\"` group -- no script, just a collision target |\n| `main.gd` | Loads the quest resource into QuestManager at startup |\n\n### The key bug to note:\nIn `projectile.gd` line 31, the call:\n```gdscript\nquest_manager.progress_quest(\"shoot_em_up_quest\", \"kill\")\n```\nuses wrong IDs. The quest ID is `\"shoot_em_up\"` and the step ID is `\"kill_step\"`. The correct call would be:\n```gdscript\nquest_manager.progress_quest(\"shoot_em_up\", \"kill_step\")\n```\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f235c04d7ffeySlJ7ac94Jd7Mh","sessionId":"ses_f235bc644ffeu7yNz1Zo5kqPBC","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790408145342,"end":1790408252525}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_818b2e74-6bf4-49f7-9fce-934456a9cb6f"}},"id":"prt_0dca439ac001tvxgg3pMGNU1Vn","sessionID":"ses_f235c04d7ffeySlJ7ac94Jd7Mh","messageID":"msg_0dca3fd32001ZF6IEkC1d8Fpr9"}}
